The Northstar Sprint — Go-Live Readiness Note
Support Deflection MVP (Node.js CLI chatbot) — handoff to Northstar's support team, no engineer from our team in the room. Replaces an earlier browser-based concept; team built a CLI instead, staying in plain Node.js.
How to run it
No install beyond Node.js. In the project folder, run: node bot-cli.js
Type a question in plain English (e.g. "where is my order ORD-78432"). Type 'exit' or 'quit' to stop.
What works today
Ticket type	Status	Owner
Order status	Working end-to-end. Handles tracking, shipping, delivery-time, and late/not-received questions against 3 mock orders (ORD-XXXXX). Gracefully handles empty input, bad format, and not-found cases.	Morris
Returns & refunds	Working end-to-end. Handles return and refund-status questions against 3 mock records (RET-XXXXX). Escalates exchanges/wrong-item requests; asks for clarification on ambiguous input.	Anne
Stock availability	Not built — scoped as a stretch goal; team prioritized the other two categories instead.	Kibet
Known-broken / out of scope
• Stock availability not built. Dataset is mocked (3 orders, 3 returns), hardcoded — not connected to real Northstar systems.
• No authentication — anyone running the script can look up any order/return. No logging. Single-session only, no shared backend.
• Routing is keyword-based (word-boundary matching); unclear questions get a clarifying fallback instead of a guess.
For Northstar's team to pick this up
1. Confirm Node.js is installed (node --version).
2. Replace mock data in orderstatus.js / returns-refunds.js with real order/inventory data.
3. To add stock availability: build stockAvailability.js following the same getResponse() pattern, then wire it into bot-cli.js's routing.
4. Add authentication before pointing this at real customer data.
5. A browser version would need a new interaction layer — the category logic itself is reusable as-is.
